────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The corpus is entirely synthetic. It contains no real government documents,
no real agency records, and no personal data. Agency names, activity codes,
and figures were generated from a fixed lexicon with seed 20260815. Some
place names used in the lexicon are real Thai subdistrict names; no real
organisation's records, and no individual person, is represented.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MODEL OUTPUTS — data/raw/ only
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The 54 files under data/raw/ are verbatim responses produced by three
third-party commercial LLM services in August 2026. They are published here
so that the scoring can be checked without re-running any model.

We are not able to place these files under CC BY 4.0, because CC BY 4.0
grants downstream users rights we do not hold. All three providers assign
output ownership to the user, or do not claim it, so publishing the files is
permitted; but all three also restrict one specific downstream use, and that
restriction travels with the files:

  OpenAI    "Use Output to develop models that compete with OpenAI" is
            prohibited.  (Terms of Use, "What you cannot do")
  Anthropic Using the Services "to develop any products or services that
            compete with our Services, including to develop or train any
            artificial intelligence or machine learning algorithms or
            models" is prohibited.  (Consumer Terms of Service)
  Google    "using AI-generated content from our services to develop
            machine learning models or related AI technology" is
            prohibited.  (Google Terms of Service, "Abusing our services")

Accordingly, data/raw/ is published under these conditions:

  1. You may read, quote, redistribute and analyse these files, including
     for research and for verifying the results in the paper, with
     attribution.
  2. You may NOT use them to train, fine-tune, distil, evaluate-for-training
     or otherwise develop any machine learning model or related AI
     technology.
  3. You may not present their content as human-written.
  4. Google's restriction is the broadest of the three and is not limited to
     competing models. If you are unsure which file came from which service,
     the model is named in every filename and in run_log.csv.

Condition 2 is a restriction of the providers, not of ours. Nothing here
grants you rights against those providers' terms; check them yourself
before any use beyond reading and verification.

Terms consulted, August 2026:
  https://openai.com/policies/row-terms-of-use/
  https://www.anthropic.com/legal/consumer-terms
  https://policies.google.com/terms
